  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="cmi-level-7-assignment-help-faq">CMI Level 7 Assignment Help — Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the word count for a CMI Level 7 strategic paper?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>The standard range is 5,000–6,500 words per unit. Some reflective units (such as Unit 701)
            specify a shorter range of 3,500–4,500 words. The word count applies to the body of the
            strategic paper — the executive summary (200–250 words), reference list, and appendices
            are excluded. Always check your specific unit brief as training providers may set variations
            within the CMI guidelines.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the difference between CMI Level 7 and a Master's degree?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Both are RQF Level 7 qualifications. The CMI Level 7 Diploma is work-based, assessed
            entirely by assignment, and can be completed alongside a full-time senior leadership role.
            A Master's degree is a taught academic programme with modules, lectures, and a research
            dissertation. The Level 7 Diploma leads to FCMI membership. Some students complete both —
            using CMI Level 7 to develop strategic management competency alongside or instead of a
            traditional MBA or MSc.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What is the difference between Critically Analyse (Level 7) and Critically Evaluate (Level 6)?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Critically Evaluate (Level 6) interrogates individual frameworks: apply them, examine
            their assumptions, consider alternatives, reach a justified conclusion. Critically Analyse
            (Level 7) interrogates the theoretical and strategic landscape as a whole — engaging with
            the academic debate in the field, not just applying established theories but understanding
            where the field is contested. A Level 7 Distinction response is unrecognisable as a Level 6
            response; it operates at a different academic register.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">How many peer-reviewed sources are needed for a CMI Level 7 assignment?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>15–20 peer-reviewed sources minimum. ManagementDirect alone is insufficient at Level 7.
            Theoretical frameworks must be cited from primary academic sources — Porter (1980), Christensen
            (1997), Barney (1991) — not textbook summaries. A bibliography that is predominantly
            ManagementDirect with a few journals will not meet Distinction standard.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Which CMI Level 7 units are most commonly selected for the Diploma?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>The most commonly selected are Unit 701 (Personal and Professional Development as a
            Strategic Leader), Unit 702 (Ethical Organisational Leadership), Unit 704 (Strategic Risk
            and Resilience), Unit 705 (Strategic Management of Resources), and Unit 708 (Innovation and
            Change Management at a Strategic Level). Unit 715 (Strategic Leadership in the Public Sector)
            is the most selected unit among NHS students.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Do you provide CMI 702 assignment help specifically?</summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <p>Yes. Unit 702 (Ethical Organisational Leadership) is one of our most requested Level 7
